Designing and operating safe chemical reaction processes — HSE HSG143 (@ic-hse-reactions: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_4W5NNM3T7AY4AWFT30RZRJQAST
Health and Safety Executive. Designing and operating safe chemical reaction processes, HSG143, first published 2000; the online PDF notes a 2008 reprint. ISBN 9780717610518. [Publisher page](https://www.hse.gov.uk/pubns/books/hsg143.htm) · [Complete authorized 64-page guide](https://www.hse.gov.uk/pubns/priced/hsg143.pdf).

Read the entire technical guide for batch/semi-batch reaction development, measurement of reaction behavior, scale, heat removal, accumulation, decomposition and the actual basis for operation and protection. Tie its methods to the chemistry, uncertainty and setting of a specific professional study rather than treating a generic nominal operating point as sufficient evidence.

The official full text, title/date and technical scope were inspected on 29 October 2026. HSE's site states OGL v3 subject to exceptions; the historical PDF carries its own Crown copyright/reproduction notice, which must be preserved rather than overwritten by an assumed licence. Its dated legal references are not asserted to describe every current jurisdiction. No guide or image is bundled.

